<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Accounts
receivables, net mainly represent amounts due from customers, including the funds extended by the Group to qualified customers, including
the merchants, through its factoring arrangements (the &#8220;factoring receivables&#8221;) and are recorded net of allowance for credit losses. As of December 31, 2024 and 2025, the balance of the factoring receivables was RMB <span id="xdx_90D_ecustom--FactoringReceivables_iI_pn3n3_uRMB_c20241231_zk4e03hdQmRa" title="Factoring receivables"><ix:nonFraction name="YJ:FactoringReceivables" contextRef="AsOf2024-12-31" id="Fact001530" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="RMB">28,149</ix:nonFraction></span> and RMB <span id="xdx_901_ecustom--FactoringReceivables_iI_pn3n3_uRMB_c20251231_zb9zk0ZLoeFa" title="Factoring receivables"><ix:nonFraction name="YJ:FactoringReceivables" contextRef="AsOf2025-12-31" id="Fact001532" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="RMB">28,090</ix:nonFraction></span>, respectively
(Note 5).</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

