June 2010, the RMB has fluctuated against the US$, at times significantly and unpredictably. The appreciation of the RMB against the
US$ was approximately <span id="xdx_908_ecustom--PercentageOfIncreasedecreaseInForeignCurrencyExchangeRateTranslation_pid_dp_c20230101__20231231_zOfebU1cetP" title="Increase in foreign currency exchange rate"><ix:nonFraction name="YJ:PercentageOfIncreasedecreaseInForeignCurrencyExchangeRateTranslation" contextRef="From2023-01-012023-12-31" id="Fact001679" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">1.70</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_901_ecustom--PercentageOfIncreasedecreaseInForeignCurrencyExchangeRateTranslation_pid_dp_c20240101__20241231_zeMmNMxNpS9e" title="Increase in foreign currency exchange rate"><ix:nonFraction name="YJ:PercentageOfIncreasedecreaseInForeignCurrencyExchangeRateTranslation" contextRef="From2024-01-012024-12-31" id="Fact001681" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">1.49</ix:nonFraction></span>% and <span id="xdx_908_ecustom--PercentageOfIncreasedecreaseInForeignCurrencyExchangeRateTranslation_pid_dp_c20250101__20251231_zsxKHdwQIgzk" title="Increase in foreign currency exchange rate"><ix:nonFraction name="YJ:PercentageOfIncreasedecreaseInForeignCurrencyExchangeRateTranslation" contextRef="From2025-01-01to2025-12-31" id="Fact001683" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">2.22</ix:nonFraction></span>% for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025, respectively. It is difficult to predict
how market forces or PRC or U.S. government policy may impact the exchange rate between the RMB and the US$ in the future.</span></p>

